1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,000
<font color="#FF8040">{\an8}Downloaded From MoviesMod.Org</font>

2
00:00:11,886 --> 00:00:14,806
Gentlemen, I'm gonna need you
to bring your A game

3
00:00:14,889 --> 00:00:17,017
if we're gonna beat Aurelita
again in the final.

4
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:20,854
I mean, they're gonna be out for blood,
and we're gonna be on their turf.

5
00:00:20,937 --> 00:00:22,814
So don't think
just 'cause we beat them once

6
00:00:22,897 --> 00:00:24,733
this is going to be an easy ride.

7
00:00:25,316 --> 00:00:27,861
I need every single one of you
to bring it.

8
00:00:28,737 --> 00:00:31,239
So go home. Get some rest.
I'll see you tomorrow.

9
00:00:31,322 --> 00:00:33,199
-Let's go, boys.
-Thanks, Coach.

10
00:00:33,283 --> 00:00:35,660
Thanks, Coach.

11
00:00:36,286 --> 00:00:37,287
All right.

12
00:00:45,211 --> 00:00:46,713
What do you think of our chances?

13
00:00:46,796 --> 00:00:49,758
I mean, if Dylan keeps his form up,
I think we got one.

14
00:00:50,383 --> 00:00:53,636
You know, I don't know how his dad
persuaded Principal Whitmore

15
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:57,307
to let him back on the team,
but to be honest, I'm kinda glad he did.

16
00:00:57,390 --> 00:01:00,310
Since we lost you,
he's pretty much all we got.

17
00:01:15,033 --> 00:01:16,951
I always help my dad
organize the food stall,

18
00:01:17,035 --> 00:01:19,287
so I'll be there from around 2:00 p.m.

19
00:01:19,370 --> 00:01:21,623
Right. Maybe I can help
show them where to set up.

20
00:01:21,706 --> 00:01:23,500
That's okay. We got it.

21
00:01:23,583 --> 00:01:25,335
Dad's pretty much
already arranged everything.

22
00:01:25,418 --> 00:01:26,961
I'm just there for backup.

23
00:01:27,587 --> 00:01:29,672
Okay. So, Grace, we'll go together.

24
00:01:29,756 --> 00:01:31,508
Yeah. Well, actually,
I'm getting there early

25
00:01:31,591 --> 00:01:32,884
to set up the church raffle.

26
00:01:33,384 --> 00:01:34,677
I could do that. What time?

27
00:01:34,761 --> 00:01:36,846
I mean, we've got plenty of volunteers.

28
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:39,974
I'll just see you when you get there?
You should probably take it easy for once.

29
00:01:40,058 --> 00:01:42,018
Yeah. Just enjoy your day.

30
00:01:43,061 --> 00:01:44,604
-Okay.
-What is it?

31
00:01:45,105 --> 00:01:47,774
I guess I'm just looking for
a distraction.

32
00:01:47,857 --> 00:01:50,401
I have my driver's test in the morning,
and I'm really nervous.

33
00:01:50,485 --> 00:01:52,112
I have to pass this time.

34
00:01:52,195 --> 00:01:53,446
You will. You'll do great.

35
00:01:54,197 --> 00:01:55,031
Yeah, I hope so.

36
00:01:55,615 --> 00:01:57,033
-I'm gonna head out.
-I'm coming.

37
00:01:57,117 --> 00:01:58,993
-Okay. Perfect.
-You got this, Jackie.

38
00:01:59,869 --> 00:02:00,870
-Bye.
-See you.

39
00:02:03,289 --> 00:02:05,083
Come on!

40
00:02:21,599 --> 00:02:22,475
Any notes?

41
00:02:23,143 --> 00:02:24,477
You know what, Walter?

42
00:02:24,561 --> 00:02:26,563
You're looking like
a real rider out there.

43
00:02:26,646 --> 00:02:28,940
I'm impressed.

44
00:02:29,023 --> 00:02:33,069
You think I'm, uh, gonna be ready
for the tryouts tomorrow?

45
00:02:33,153 --> 00:02:35,155
I really need that sponsorship.

46
00:02:35,238 --> 00:02:37,615
Yeah. I wouldn't let you
go out there if I didn't.

47
00:02:37,699 --> 00:02:40,535
It's my reputation on the line too.

48
00:02:41,995 --> 00:02:44,622
You've come a long way, Alex Walter.

49
00:02:44,706 --> 00:02:48,459
Yeah, well, it's pretty much
all thanks to you, right?

50
00:02:48,543 --> 00:02:51,004
Look, I'll take the credit,
but you've put the work in.

51
00:02:51,087 --> 00:02:54,299
Long hours, early mornings.
I can coach you all day long.

52
00:02:54,382 --> 00:02:56,384
But you're the only one
who can make yourself better.

53
00:02:57,177 --> 00:02:58,845
And you've done that.

54
00:03:00,847 --> 00:03:02,682
Why does that sound like a goodbye?

55
00:03:03,433 --> 00:03:07,687
If my dad decides to sponsor you tomorrow,
then I won't be your trainer anymore.

56
00:03:14,068 --> 00:03:15,486
That was hilarious.

57
00:03:18,489 --> 00:03:20,742
Yo, I'll catch up with you guys later.

58
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:25,496
Why are you still here?

59
00:03:26,331 --> 00:03:28,249
I'm trying to finish these
to sell at the Sparkle.

60
00:03:28,333 --> 00:03:30,501
Oh. Cute.

61
00:03:32,795 --> 00:03:35,173
So, you're still not talking to me, huh?

62
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:42,138
What do you want me to say, Dylan?

63
00:03:43,932 --> 00:03:46,559
Did you think I'd be okay with you
trying to cheat on a drug test

64
00:03:46,643 --> 00:03:48,686
and then getting your dad
to bribe the school?

65
00:03:48,770 --> 00:03:50,480
He didn't bribe the school.

66
00:03:50,563 --> 00:03:52,357
But he still made everything okay, right?

67
00:03:54,108 --> 00:03:55,526
Look, I was desperate.

68
00:03:56,027 --> 00:03:58,655
Okay, if I don't play, then I might not
get to go to the showcase.

69
00:03:58,738 --> 00:04:01,366
If I don't get into the showcase,
then I don't play college football.

70
00:04:01,449 --> 00:04:06,162
And if I don't do that, my dad
will not speak to me till I'm like… 40.

71
00:04:06,996 --> 00:04:07,956
So?

72
00:04:08,831 --> 00:04:11,668
Is that all that matters?
You being a good boy for your daddy?

73
00:04:13,169 --> 00:04:14,963
Why don't you stand up to him?

74
00:04:15,046 --> 00:04:17,006
Don't you want to be your own person?

75
00:04:19,092 --> 00:04:20,426
I don't know if I can.

76
00:04:23,972 --> 00:04:25,390
I have to finish these.

77
00:04:53,084 --> 00:04:54,127
That was perfect.

78
00:04:55,044 --> 00:04:56,921
-I think you got it.
-Really?

79
00:04:57,588 --> 00:04:58,881
Absolutely.

80
00:04:59,549 --> 00:05:01,592
You're gonna pass this time, 100%.

81
00:05:02,885 --> 00:05:04,095
Positive vibes only.

82
00:05:04,178 --> 00:05:05,596
Okay.

83
00:05:06,973 --> 00:05:08,641
-Hey, bud.
-Hi.

84
00:05:09,726 --> 00:05:10,727
Hi.

85
00:05:12,103 --> 00:05:13,021
How's it going?

86
00:05:14,314 --> 00:05:15,189
It's going.

87
00:05:16,858 --> 00:05:18,318
Big game tomorrow, huh?

88
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:20,194
Yep.

89
00:05:20,778 --> 00:05:21,904
Well, you'll do great.

90
00:05:31,706 --> 00:05:35,626
Um, I haven't seen you much
since Halloween.

91
00:05:37,670 --> 00:05:39,172
Yeah, I know.

92
00:05:40,048 --> 00:05:43,176
You know, Tony's, coaching,
and studying. It's just kinda--

93
00:05:43,259 --> 00:05:45,470
Have you gotten
your new SAT scores back yet?

94
00:05:46,721 --> 00:05:47,555
No.

95
00:05:47,638 --> 00:05:48,514
Oh.

96
00:05:49,015 --> 00:05:51,601
I feel like they should've come through.
Maybe you should call.

97
00:05:51,684 --> 00:05:54,479
Yeah, you're right. I will. Thanks.

98
00:05:57,273 --> 00:05:59,359
Do you wanna work on
college applications together

99
00:05:59,442 --> 00:06:00,526
like we talked about?

100
00:06:01,444 --> 00:06:03,321
No. That's okay.

101
00:06:03,404 --> 00:06:05,740
We're kind of running out of time.

102
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:09,202
-I mean, I could do a first pass for you--
-Jackie, just leave it.

103
00:06:10,119 --> 00:06:11,746
I gotta get back to these plays.

104
00:06:12,246 --> 00:06:14,040
Like you said, tomorrow's a big day.

105
00:06:15,124 --> 00:06:16,042
So…

106
00:06:17,502 --> 00:06:19,212
Okay. Good luck.

107
00:06:20,630 --> 00:06:21,631
Yeah.

108
00:06:23,007 --> 00:06:24,008
You too.

109
00:06:52,328 --> 00:06:54,205
-Hi.
-Oh my God.

110
00:06:54,288 --> 00:06:56,124
Surprise!

111
00:06:56,833 --> 00:06:57,708
Oh.

112
00:06:58,626 --> 00:07:00,962
Did I get it wrong?
Weren't you coming in next week?

113
00:07:01,045 --> 00:07:04,757
No, you didn't. Honestly, babe,
you sounded like you really needed a hug.

114
00:07:04,841 --> 00:07:08,261
So I told Felix I needed to leave
a week early, and it's all good.

115
00:07:13,808 --> 00:07:16,394
You have no idea how much I missed you.

116
00:07:23,818 --> 00:07:25,528
Okay.

117
00:07:26,487 --> 00:07:27,488
Good luck.

118
00:07:31,075 --> 00:07:32,952
Oh, come on. You got this.

119
00:07:33,035 --> 00:07:35,496
And I'm gonna be right here
waiting when you're done.

120
00:07:36,831 --> 00:07:37,665
I promise.

121
00:07:37,748 --> 00:07:38,583
Okay.

122
00:07:43,296 --> 00:07:44,797
You're gonna crush it.

123
00:07:53,222 --> 00:07:54,307
Good to see you.

124
00:07:59,645 --> 00:08:01,189
There's, like, a ton of riders here.

125
00:08:01,272 --> 00:08:03,232
You think you'd get a pass
'cause I trained you?

126
00:08:03,816 --> 00:08:05,067
Don't get cocky.

127
00:08:05,151 --> 00:08:07,528
This won't be easy. It's a big deal.

128
00:08:07,612 --> 00:08:10,615
If you get this gig,
it'll be a lot of work.

129
00:08:10,698 --> 00:08:14,744
Even more than you're used to right now.
And it's gonna be nights, weekends away.

130
00:08:14,827 --> 00:08:17,288
Are you sure you want that?
Because if you don't…

131
00:08:17,371 --> 00:08:18,539
Yeah, I want it.

132
00:08:20,374 --> 00:08:22,251
You think Jackie will be happy with that?

133
00:08:24,212 --> 00:08:25,922
-What do you mean?
-Come on, Alex.

134
00:08:26,005 --> 00:08:27,089
I know you two are together.

135
00:08:27,173 --> 00:08:29,383
What I don't get
is why it's such a secret.

136
00:08:29,467 --> 00:08:30,676
I mean, what are you afraid of?

137
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:33,221
I'm not afraid. It's just complicated.

138
00:08:33,304 --> 00:08:36,724
Look, if you wanna keep going with this,
you should know that it's not easy

139
00:08:36,807 --> 00:08:39,060
to have a relationship
with someone who's not in our world.

140
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:41,354
Not even if that relationship
is rock solid.

141
00:08:41,437 --> 00:08:42,813
-So if it isn't--
-But it is.

142
00:08:44,649 --> 00:08:46,359
So there's nothing to worry about.

143
00:08:47,693 --> 00:08:48,778
Okay, then.

144
00:08:49,904 --> 00:08:50,863
Let's go, cowboy.

145
00:08:50,947 --> 00:08:52,156
Mm-hmm.

146
00:08:58,788 --> 00:08:59,664
You ready?

147
00:09:00,289 --> 00:09:02,583
Well, I, uh, guess we'll find out, right?

148
00:09:05,836 --> 00:09:08,548
All right, Isaac.
You good? All right, let's do it.

149
00:09:09,048 --> 00:09:09,882
Hey, Cole.

150
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:13,469
Listen. I'm not playing today.

151
00:09:14,637 --> 00:09:16,097
What are you talking about?

152
00:09:16,180 --> 00:09:18,307
I have to take responsibility
for what I did.

153
00:09:18,391 --> 00:09:20,643
I can't keep having my dad
clean up my messes.

154
00:09:21,769 --> 00:09:23,938
I get this isn't great timing.

155
00:09:24,522 --> 00:09:25,856
Uh, you think?

156
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:26,774
I'm sorry.

157
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:30,361
Really, man,
I hate that I'm letting the team down,

158
00:09:30,444 --> 00:09:33,573
but I should've never agreed to this.

159
00:09:35,074 --> 00:09:37,201
I'm just trying to do
the right thing, okay?

160
00:09:37,285 --> 00:09:39,036
Isn't it a little bit late for that?

161
00:09:39,745 --> 00:09:43,874
Yes. But this should be Isaac's game.

162
00:09:43,958 --> 00:09:47,336
Dylan, it's the division finals.
The team needs you.

163
00:09:48,421 --> 00:09:49,255
No.

164
00:09:50,339 --> 00:09:51,549
They need you.

165
00:10:05,187 --> 00:10:06,272
Thanks.

166
00:10:07,773 --> 00:10:09,108
-Yes!
-I passed!

167
00:10:10,735 --> 00:10:12,820
Yes! I knew you would.

168
00:10:17,283 --> 00:10:18,784
Oh my God. Is that…

169
00:10:18,868 --> 00:10:20,620
Your mom's car. Yep.

170
00:10:21,704 --> 00:10:23,289
Richard had it shipped out from New York.

171
00:10:23,372 --> 00:10:25,625
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

172
00:10:27,001 --> 00:10:29,086
Wait. What would you
have done if I failed again?

173
00:10:29,170 --> 00:10:31,005
No, we knew you weren't gonna fail.

174
00:10:31,922 --> 00:10:35,593
But if you did, we would've just taken it
back to Tony's garage like the last time.

175
00:10:36,969 --> 00:10:38,179
Okay.

176
00:10:39,388 --> 00:10:40,348
Go on, then.

177
00:10:42,224 --> 00:10:43,059
Thank you.

178
00:10:43,142 --> 00:10:44,894
You're welcome. Have fun.

179
00:10:46,479 --> 00:10:47,355
Be safe.

180
00:11:11,087 --> 00:11:12,213
Whoa!

181
00:11:16,634 --> 00:11:19,053
No, he won't play.
It's gonna have to be Isaac.

182
00:11:19,136 --> 00:11:20,763
Okay, gentlemen, listen up.

183
00:11:22,139 --> 00:11:24,642
Isaac, you need
to warm up your throwing arm.

184
00:11:24,725 --> 00:11:27,311
-What?
-You're gonna be our quarterback today.

185
00:11:27,395 --> 00:11:32,108
Yeah, our, uh… our number 19,
Mr. Newsome, will not be playing today.

186
00:11:32,191 --> 00:11:33,984
Coach! Coach!

187
00:11:34,068 --> 00:11:37,279
Okay, settle down. Settle down.
It'll be fine. It'll be fine.

188
00:11:37,363 --> 00:11:40,116
He decided to take
his suspension seriously.

189
00:11:40,741 --> 00:11:43,994
Hey. Come on, guys. Just do your best.

190
00:11:45,121 --> 00:11:46,914
Just do your best. Come on.

191
00:11:47,707 --> 00:11:49,458
Okay? Let's go! Let's go! Let's go!

192
00:11:49,542 --> 00:11:51,919
-We got a football game to win.
-We got this.

193
00:11:57,216 --> 00:11:58,050
Dylan!

194
00:12:00,052 --> 00:12:01,345
What the hell are you doing?

195
00:12:03,639 --> 00:12:04,890
I was suspended, Dad.

196
00:12:05,725 --> 00:12:06,976
-I shouldn't play.
-What?

197
00:12:07,059 --> 00:12:09,979
After everything I did
to get you back on that team?

198
00:12:10,062 --> 00:12:12,523
-Do you have any idea how hard that was?
-I know.

199
00:12:13,524 --> 00:12:14,525
And I'm sorry.

200
00:12:15,484 --> 00:12:20,406
Failing a drug test, you paying
to keep me on the team, it's not right.

201
00:12:21,198 --> 00:12:22,199
I messed up.

202
00:12:23,117 --> 00:12:25,161
I should have to face
the consequences, right? I mean,

203
00:12:25,244 --> 00:12:27,788
otherwise, what does anything matter?

204
00:12:27,872 --> 00:12:29,623
What matters is you playing football.

205
00:12:29,707 --> 00:12:32,501
-Maybe even going pro one day.
-That's your dream, Dad.

206
00:12:34,462 --> 00:12:35,463
It's not mine.

207
00:12:36,672 --> 00:12:39,717
Okay, and I'm sorry
that it didn't work out for you.

208
00:12:41,343 --> 00:12:42,720
But this isn't what I want.

209
00:12:45,097 --> 00:12:46,474
At least not like this.

210
00:12:54,148 --> 00:12:55,149
You know what?

211
00:12:58,569 --> 00:13:00,613
You're probably not D1 material anyway.

212
00:13:22,510 --> 00:13:24,386
Some like to put on business suits…

213
00:13:24,470 --> 00:13:26,347
-You're up, Alex.
-Don't worry.

214
00:13:27,223 --> 00:13:28,432
I got this.

215
00:13:28,516 --> 00:13:30,184
Them jeans and boots

216
00:13:32,603 --> 00:13:34,188
Turn it up country

217
00:13:34,271 --> 00:13:37,107
Swing a little in the backwoods
Outside of town

218
00:13:37,191 --> 00:13:38,651
Turn it up country…

219
00:13:38,734 --> 00:13:39,652
Yah!

220
00:13:42,238 --> 00:13:44,573
Light up the bonfire
Light up the stake

221
00:13:44,657 --> 00:13:47,159
Don't come with your whiskey straight

222
00:13:47,243 --> 00:13:49,662
My friend, trouble
You just might find

223
00:13:49,745 --> 00:13:51,539
A Tennessee honey

224
00:13:52,039 --> 00:13:55,417
When you turn it up country

225
00:13:57,127 --> 00:14:00,506
Yeah, we'll turn it up country

226
00:14:07,054 --> 00:14:07,888
Hut!

227
00:14:09,348 --> 00:14:11,225
Come on, Garcia, pass him the ball!

228
00:14:11,308 --> 00:14:14,144
He wasn't ready, your cousin.

229
00:14:16,981 --> 00:14:18,274
Hold on, I gotta take this.

230
00:14:19,483 --> 00:14:22,319
Honey, you okay?
I'm in the middle of the game.

231
00:14:22,987 --> 00:14:24,947
What? How far apart are they?

232
00:14:25,030 --> 00:14:27,783
Right, okay. Yeah, I'll be right there.

233
00:14:28,576 --> 00:14:29,702
Call your ma!

234
00:14:32,079 --> 00:14:33,372
Okay, uh,

235
00:14:33,455 --> 00:14:34,748
my wife is in labor.

236
00:14:34,832 --> 00:14:37,501
-I have to go.
-Wait, but what about the game?

237
00:14:37,585 --> 00:14:39,211
No, you… you… you gotta take over.

238
00:14:39,295 --> 00:14:41,422
-No, I can't do that.
-Of course you can.

239
00:14:41,505 --> 00:14:43,883
Just run the plays
like we practiced, all right?

240
00:14:43,966 --> 00:14:46,844
And keep their spirits up.
I'm counting on you.

241
00:14:47,428 --> 00:14:48,429
We all are.

242
00:15:03,277 --> 00:15:05,029
Congratulations, driver.

243
00:15:05,738 --> 00:15:06,906
Nice ride.

244
00:15:06,989 --> 00:15:09,116
Thanks. It was my mom's car.

245
00:15:09,992 --> 00:15:12,036
It's so you. Can you take this?

246
00:15:12,119 --> 00:15:13,537
Yeah, of course.

247
00:15:14,079 --> 00:15:15,289
So, what did Alex say?

248
00:15:15,915 --> 00:15:19,585
Uh, we kinda agreed
we wouldn't text or talk too much.

249
00:15:19,668 --> 00:15:21,211
It might look suspicious.

250
00:15:21,295 --> 00:15:23,464
Right. I mean, it's been weeks.

251
00:15:23,547 --> 00:15:25,799
When are you gonna tell people
that you're together?

252
00:15:26,550 --> 00:15:28,218
I don't know. Soon, I guess.

253
00:15:29,345 --> 00:15:31,931
But I thought you two said
"I love you" to each other already,

254
00:15:32,014 --> 00:15:34,767
so I don't really get
why you'd have to keep things a secret.

255
00:15:37,102 --> 00:15:38,437
Is it because of Cole?

256
00:15:38,938 --> 00:15:39,772
No.

257
00:15:40,898 --> 00:15:44,234
But Cole has been acting
a little off lately.

258
00:15:45,027 --> 00:15:47,279
We were supposed to do
college applications together,

259
00:15:47,363 --> 00:15:50,449
but he's been spending all of his time
at Tony's or at football,

260
00:15:50,532 --> 00:15:52,868
and I'm just worried
he's going to miss the deadlines.

261
00:15:53,369 --> 00:15:55,204
And I thought he had retaken the SATs,

262
00:15:55,287 --> 00:15:57,706
but he says
he hasn't gotten his results back,

263
00:15:57,790 --> 00:16:00,376
so I don't even know if he did take them.

264
00:16:00,459 --> 00:16:03,587
Maybe he did, and he just doesn't want
to tell you he did badly again.

265
00:16:03,671 --> 00:16:05,506
I don't think he'd lie to me.

266
00:16:06,507 --> 00:16:09,343
Jackie, why are you
so invested in Cole's future anyways?

267
00:16:09,843 --> 00:16:13,138
He's a big boy. He can handle it himself,
and you're with Alex.

268
00:16:13,639 --> 00:16:15,140
Cole needs me.

269
00:16:15,224 --> 00:16:17,685
Does he? Or do you need him to need you?

270
00:16:18,394 --> 00:16:19,645
What do you mean?

271
00:16:19,728 --> 00:16:21,855
I mean, maybe you should just pick a boy.

272
00:16:25,401 --> 00:16:26,402
Sorry.

273
00:16:27,027 --> 00:16:29,071
You know what?
I would love it if my biggest problem

274
00:16:29,154 --> 00:16:30,948
was which hot boy likes me best,

275
00:16:31,031 --> 00:16:34,368
but not that there's anything going on
in my love life, of course.

276
00:16:36,662 --> 00:16:38,414
Grace, is everything okay?

277
00:16:38,497 --> 00:16:39,707
No.

278
00:16:41,417 --> 00:16:44,503
My dad moved out.
My parents might be getting a divorce.

279
00:16:45,087 --> 00:16:46,171
I didn't know.

280
00:16:46,255 --> 00:16:47,756
Yeah, of course you didn't.

281
00:16:49,133 --> 00:16:50,092
I'm really sorry.

282
00:16:50,175 --> 00:16:51,093
It's fine.

283
00:16:51,885 --> 00:16:53,137
It's okay, really.

284
00:16:54,179 --> 00:16:57,141
-I gotta finish setting up the raffle.
-Are you sure I can't help?

285
00:16:57,224 --> 00:16:58,475
No, thanks. I got it.

286
00:17:04,106 --> 00:17:05,941
Hut!

287
00:17:09,111 --> 00:17:11,655
Silver Falls just can't catch a break.

288
00:17:15,117 --> 00:17:17,703
Wolves touchdown by number 37.

289
00:17:20,164 --> 00:17:22,082
Wolves ball, first down.

290
00:17:26,503 --> 00:17:30,507
Big tackle. Number 97,
Hughes on the 50-yard line.

291
00:17:31,884 --> 00:17:36,764
And we are going into halftime
with Aurelita in the lead.

292
00:17:37,347 --> 00:17:40,768
Silver Falls are gonna have to work hard
to pull this back.

293
00:17:42,603 --> 00:17:45,981
And now a very special halftime show.

294
00:17:46,065 --> 00:17:50,069
Fans, let me hear you make some noise
for the team cheerleaders

295
00:17:50,152 --> 00:17:52,029
from the Silver Falls Bighorns…

296
00:17:52,112 --> 00:17:53,072
You okay?

297
00:17:53,906 --> 00:17:54,990
What do you think?

298
00:17:58,160 --> 00:17:59,787
They'd be better off without me.

299
00:18:00,621 --> 00:18:04,124
It's like you said, I was just…
I was just Allen's little bitch.

300
00:18:05,167 --> 00:18:06,877
I don't know what I'm doing.

301
00:18:08,212 --> 00:18:09,505
So, what? You gonna quit?

302
00:18:10,839 --> 00:18:11,799
You did.

303
00:18:13,300 --> 00:18:14,885
Yeah, but you're the coach.

304
00:18:16,178 --> 00:18:18,055
-I can't do this.
-Wow.

305
00:18:18,847 --> 00:18:20,641
You're really giving up that easy, huh?

306
00:18:21,433 --> 00:18:23,560
You think any of this has been easy?

307
00:18:24,061 --> 00:18:26,605
You think I wanted to coach
the team I used to lead?

308
00:18:27,106 --> 00:18:28,482
Being on the sidelines?

309
00:18:28,565 --> 00:18:31,485
Watching you throw away
all these chances I wish I still had?

310
00:18:34,571 --> 00:18:35,781
I'm not giving up easy.

311
00:18:35,864 --> 00:18:39,952
I'm giving up the way I do everything.
As hard as I can.

312
00:18:44,248 --> 00:18:45,249
You done?

313
00:18:49,086 --> 00:18:50,087
Look, man.

314
00:18:50,838 --> 00:18:53,382
I know it's been rough,
but you're a good coach.

315
00:18:53,966 --> 00:18:56,093
The team knows that.
You just gotta know it too.

316
00:18:56,677 --> 00:18:59,847
Look, the guys have been giving
you shit because you're letting them.

317
00:19:00,514 --> 00:19:01,515
Me walking away…

318
00:19:03,392 --> 00:19:04,434
they'll get over it.

319
00:19:05,602 --> 00:19:06,603
But you?

320
00:19:08,355 --> 00:19:10,941
Nah, man. They look up to you.

321
00:19:12,234 --> 00:19:13,652
They really do need you.

322
00:19:15,237 --> 00:19:19,366
And one of us should take responsibility
for what happens to this team today.

323
00:19:32,963 --> 00:19:34,047
Go get 'em, Coach.

324
00:19:41,013 --> 00:19:42,014
Hey, guys!

325
00:19:43,015 --> 00:19:45,225
Hey, everybody! Come on.

326
00:19:46,101 --> 00:19:48,270
Everyone. Guys, quiet.

327
00:19:48,353 --> 00:19:50,063
Hey! Come on.

328
00:19:50,689 --> 00:19:51,899
Quiet!

329
00:19:52,733 --> 00:19:54,902
Make some noise for the team cheerleaders…

330
00:19:54,985 --> 00:19:57,654
Okay, listen to me.

331
00:19:58,906 --> 00:20:01,658
I'm not gonna lie.
It's tough out there today.

332
00:20:01,742 --> 00:20:03,076
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

333
00:20:03,577 --> 00:20:04,536
But we're tough.

334
00:20:06,163 --> 00:20:07,873
We've been through much worse than this.

335
00:20:08,373 --> 00:20:11,543
But right now we're playing scared,
and they can smell it on us.

336
00:20:11,627 --> 00:20:13,837
Because our only hope
walked away just before the game.

337
00:20:13,921 --> 00:20:15,464
Forget about that! Okay?

338
00:20:15,547 --> 00:20:17,716
Okay, no one's responsible
for how this team is playing

339
00:20:17,799 --> 00:20:20,135
except every player right here, right now.

340
00:20:20,886 --> 00:20:23,430
The best times of my life
have been with this team,

341
00:20:23,931 --> 00:20:25,807
so Iknowwe can do this.

342
00:20:25,891 --> 00:20:26,975
I know you.

343
00:20:27,851 --> 00:20:31,563
Jay, Dante, when you two work together,
you're unstoppable.

344
00:20:31,647 --> 00:20:33,023
We rely on you.

345
00:20:33,774 --> 00:20:37,611
And TJ, if you run like I know you can,
nobody's gonna catch you.

346
00:20:37,694 --> 00:20:39,988
And the rest of you? You're a team.

347
00:20:41,615 --> 00:20:42,699
You're my team.

348
00:20:43,909 --> 00:20:47,287
We're Bighorns.
So let's show 'em what that means!

349
00:20:48,538 --> 00:20:50,707
-Are you guys with me?
-Yes, Coach.

350
00:20:50,791 --> 00:20:53,126
-I said, are you with me?
-Yes, Coach!

351
00:20:55,587 --> 00:20:56,421
Okay!

352
00:20:57,089 --> 00:20:59,675
Jay, do the honors. Break us down.

353
00:21:00,968 --> 00:21:01,969
Bighorns on three!

354
00:21:02,052 --> 00:21:03,887
-One, two, three, Bighorns!
-Bighorns!

355
00:21:03,971 --> 00:21:05,555
Let's go, boys!

356
00:21:08,850 --> 00:21:09,685
Hey.

357
00:21:10,560 --> 00:21:12,771
It's just like playing at home
with Parker in the yard.

358
00:21:13,272 --> 00:21:14,606
-Right?
-Right.

359
00:21:14,690 --> 00:21:15,899
-Right?
-Right!

360
00:21:21,405 --> 00:21:23,949
Hey. Everything okay over here?

361
00:21:25,033 --> 00:21:26,410
Sure. Here you go.

362
00:21:27,953 --> 00:21:30,580
-Grace.
-I think I really upset her.

363
00:21:30,664 --> 00:21:32,207
Did you know about her parents?

364
00:21:32,291 --> 00:21:33,375
She just told me.

365
00:21:33,458 --> 00:21:36,962
-I wish she'd said something sooner.
-But that's Grace.

366
00:21:37,045 --> 00:21:39,798
She never says
if something is wrong or asks for help.

367
00:21:40,674 --> 00:21:42,801
She always puts
a brave face on everything.

368
00:21:44,428 --> 00:21:45,595
I feel terrible.

369
00:21:45,679 --> 00:21:49,057
With everything that's been going on
with Nathan and Zach,

370
00:21:49,141 --> 00:21:50,851
I've been wrapped up in myself too.

371
00:21:51,351 --> 00:21:53,103
Well, we have to make it up to her.

372
00:21:54,021 --> 00:21:55,063
Here you go. Yeah.

373
00:21:55,647 --> 00:21:56,773
Absolutely.

374
00:21:58,358 --> 00:22:01,069
Okay, cowboy. That was a great ride.

375
00:22:01,153 --> 00:22:03,989
Yeah. Yeah, it felt pretty good.

376
00:22:04,072 --> 00:22:05,490
What did your dad think?

377
00:22:06,408 --> 00:22:07,409
You're in.

378
00:22:07,951 --> 00:22:09,619
Really?

379
00:22:12,247 --> 00:22:13,457
You know what this means?

380
00:22:14,333 --> 00:22:15,542
We're teammates now.

381
00:22:17,002 --> 00:22:19,129
Do you want to come celebrate
with the rest of the guys?

382
00:22:20,422 --> 00:22:22,215
Uh… no, thanks.

383
00:22:22,966 --> 00:22:26,011
I gotta head to the Sparkle to see Jackie.

384
00:22:26,094 --> 00:22:28,013
Okay, then. Have fun.

385
00:22:30,057 --> 00:22:30,932
I'll see you soon.

386
00:22:31,892 --> 00:22:32,768
See you soon.

387
00:22:36,521 --> 00:22:38,607
Two, three, Buffalo Run!
Two, three, Buffalo Run!

388
00:22:38,690 --> 00:22:40,150
Oh, light 'em up…

389
00:22:41,777 --> 00:22:46,406
Extra point is good. Silver Falls
making an incredible comeback.

390
00:22:49,368 --> 00:22:52,162
-There we go!
-They're now in the lead.

391
00:22:54,998 --> 00:22:58,293
All right! Isaac,
you can do this. Let's go!

392
00:22:59,252 --> 00:23:02,672
And Garcia coming back
onto the field, feeling the pressure here…

393
00:23:02,756 --> 00:23:05,133
Red 16, Ginger. On two. Ready?

394
00:23:05,217 --> 00:23:06,343
Break!

395
00:23:09,513 --> 00:23:11,723
Red 16. Red 16.

396
00:23:11,807 --> 00:23:12,849
Now! Hut!

397
00:23:12,933 --> 00:23:14,893
I wanna go with it

398
00:23:14,976 --> 00:23:18,397
I wanna shake you up
And take over control of it…

399
00:23:19,022 --> 00:23:21,817
There's the throw! He catches it!

400
00:23:21,900 --> 00:23:22,984
Keep going!

401
00:23:24,569 --> 00:23:25,779
Go, Isaac!

402
00:23:25,862 --> 00:23:28,740
Past the 20, down the ten!

403
00:23:29,866 --> 00:23:33,370
It's gonna be a Silver Falls touchdown!

404
00:23:33,453 --> 00:23:36,748
What a trick play
from Assistant Coach Cole Walter.

405
00:23:37,332 --> 00:23:38,917
And they've done it.

406
00:23:39,835 --> 00:23:41,086
-Whoo!
-All right, Cole!

407
00:23:41,169 --> 00:23:43,422
-Let's go!
-Yeah, Cole, you're the man!

408
00:23:43,505 --> 00:23:45,382
Yeah, Cole! Good job, Coach!

409
00:23:45,465 --> 00:23:49,845
Isaac! Isaac! Isaac! Isaac! Isaac!

410
00:23:51,847 --> 00:23:53,098
Oh my God.

411
00:23:54,266 --> 00:23:55,934
Um, okay, I'll call you back.

412
00:23:58,937 --> 00:24:00,564
Jackie, did you hear? They won.

413
00:24:00,647 --> 00:24:02,441
Isaac scored a touchdown.
Danny just called me.

414
00:24:02,524 --> 00:24:04,609
-What? That's amazing!
-Yeah.

415
00:24:20,750 --> 00:24:23,837
Jacks, one nonalcoholic mulled wine.

416
00:24:23,920 --> 00:24:25,130
Thanks.

417
00:24:31,928 --> 00:24:34,639
Uh, I gotta go do something.

418
00:24:37,767 --> 00:24:38,602
Hi.

419
00:24:39,102 --> 00:24:41,271
Hey, Nathan. Um, how are you doing?

420
00:24:43,356 --> 00:24:44,649
I'm okay, I guess.

421
00:24:45,442 --> 00:24:46,276
Good.

422
00:24:49,529 --> 00:24:51,072
Zach wants you back, you know?

423
00:24:51,573 --> 00:24:53,033
That's what it was all about.

424
00:24:53,825 --> 00:24:55,994
He was never really into me at all.

425
00:24:56,077 --> 00:24:57,871
I did try to warn you about him.

426
00:24:58,371 --> 00:25:01,208
Zach is very good
at getting people to do what he wants.

427
00:25:02,125 --> 00:25:04,169
I really don't know what happened.

428
00:25:05,587 --> 00:25:06,796
I'm so sorry, Sky.

429
00:25:06,880 --> 00:25:08,006
I know you are.

430
00:25:09,799 --> 00:25:11,843
-I don't think you meant to hurt me.
-I really didn't.

431
00:25:11,927 --> 00:25:15,305
But I do think you didn't care enough
about not hurting me

432
00:25:15,388 --> 00:25:17,849
just because someone else
gave you some attention.

433
00:25:25,649 --> 00:25:29,819
Skylar, before I met you,
no one had ever looked at me like that.

434
00:25:31,863 --> 00:25:34,866
But even then, I felt like
I had to convince you to like me.

435
00:25:35,534 --> 00:25:36,618
To be with me.

436
00:25:36,701 --> 00:25:40,914
And I always felt like
I liked you more than you liked me.

437
00:25:41,873 --> 00:25:45,835
But with Zach,
he just made me feel so wanted.

438
00:25:45,919 --> 00:25:48,797
You being insecure
isn't an excuse for what you did.

439
00:25:48,880 --> 00:25:49,714
I know.

440
00:25:51,216 --> 00:25:52,050
I know.

441
00:25:52,592 --> 00:25:54,553
But, Sky, I didn't mean it, okay?

442
00:25:55,345 --> 00:25:59,099
-If we could just try again…
-What? You and me? I don't…

443
00:26:00,559 --> 00:26:01,393
Sky.

444
00:26:03,186 --> 00:26:04,145
I love you.

445
00:26:07,899 --> 00:26:08,942
You know what?

446
00:26:10,610 --> 00:26:11,820
I think I love you too.

447
00:26:14,072 --> 00:26:16,074
But I don't think I can trust you anymore.

448
00:26:19,411 --> 00:26:21,454
And I can't put myself through that again.

449
00:26:21,538 --> 00:26:23,123
But it would never happen a…

450
00:26:25,208 --> 00:26:26,084
Sky.

451
00:26:28,169 --> 00:26:29,212
I'm sorry.

452
00:26:57,115 --> 00:26:58,158
Grace?

453
00:27:02,412 --> 00:27:04,581
I'm so sorry.

454
00:27:05,290 --> 00:27:08,126
I had no idea
you were going through all of that.

455
00:27:08,209 --> 00:27:09,919
-It's okay.
-No, it's not.

456
00:27:10,003 --> 00:27:12,005
I've been way too wrapped up in myself.

457
00:27:12,088 --> 00:27:13,923
-No, I didn't mean that.
-It's okay.

458
00:27:14,507 --> 00:27:15,717
I needed to hear it.

459
00:27:15,800 --> 00:27:18,053
And I want to say thank you

460
00:27:18,720 --> 00:27:19,721
for everything.

461
00:27:20,680 --> 00:27:22,599
For the dance playlist.

462
00:27:22,682 --> 00:27:25,101
For driving to see the bands.

463
00:27:25,185 --> 00:27:27,395
For supporting the pop-up.

464
00:27:27,479 --> 00:27:29,856
For pushing me to run for class president.

465
00:27:29,939 --> 00:27:30,774
Yeah.

466
00:27:31,399 --> 00:27:34,319
I couldn't have done
any of those things without you.

467
00:27:37,238 --> 00:27:39,866
And I… I really want to say thank you

468
00:27:39,949 --> 00:27:43,328
for taking me for ice cream
that very first day of school.

469
00:27:44,996 --> 00:27:47,248
Yeah, well,
I can always go for ice cream, so…

470
00:27:51,127 --> 00:27:53,171
You never say
when something's bothering you.

471
00:27:54,130 --> 00:27:57,550
-Yeah, 'cause no one cares.
-That is absolutely not true.

472
00:27:58,176 --> 00:27:59,219
I care.

473
00:28:00,053 --> 00:28:01,554
Skylar cares.

474
00:28:02,889 --> 00:28:04,891
Grace, you are such a good friend,

475
00:28:04,974 --> 00:28:06,893
and I've been taking you for granted.

476
00:28:08,770 --> 00:28:09,604
And I'm…

477
00:28:10,939 --> 00:28:13,233
I'm really sorry about your parents.

478
00:28:15,402 --> 00:28:16,736
What can I do to help?

479
00:28:17,821 --> 00:28:19,322
You already did.

480
00:28:22,617 --> 00:28:24,619
Well, I'm gonna be better, okay?

481
00:28:25,161 --> 00:28:27,580
And I'm gonna make it up to you.

482
00:28:27,664 --> 00:28:30,709
Maybe next week we could go shopping,

483
00:28:30,792 --> 00:28:34,003
and you could stay at the Walters',
and we'll order pizza.

484
00:28:36,673 --> 00:28:39,134
Yeah, that sounds cool. Thanks.

485
00:28:41,428 --> 00:28:44,305
And for starters, I'm taking you on that.

486
00:28:47,600 --> 00:28:49,894
That's for children, Jackie.

487
00:28:49,978 --> 00:28:51,896
So? Come on.

488
00:28:51,980 --> 00:28:53,022
Oh God.

489
00:28:53,523 --> 00:28:54,983
Can we… can we hop on?

490
00:28:56,067 --> 00:28:57,402
-Okay, ready?
-You have to jump.

491
00:28:57,485 --> 00:28:58,778
Okay. Ah!

492
00:29:12,792 --> 00:29:14,502
Jackie, come here.

493
00:29:19,883 --> 00:29:21,176
-What?
-I did it.

494
00:29:21,259 --> 00:29:22,385
I got the sponsorship.

495
00:29:22,469 --> 00:29:24,095
-You did? That's amazing!
-Yeah.

496
00:29:25,680 --> 00:29:28,141
Wait, Alex. What are you doing?
Somebody might see.

497
00:29:28,725 --> 00:29:32,270
I don't understand
why we have to keep it a secret.

498
00:29:32,771 --> 00:29:35,899
-Why can't anyone know?
-It… it's just not the right time.

499
00:29:35,982 --> 00:29:38,777
But we can talk about it later, okay?

500
00:29:38,860 --> 00:29:41,654
But I am.
I'm… I'm really proud of you for today.

501
00:29:41,738 --> 00:29:42,822
Really.

502
00:29:55,460 --> 00:29:56,461
Hey.

503
00:29:58,588 --> 00:29:59,714
Hey.

504
00:30:01,257 --> 00:30:02,300
Congratulations.

505
00:30:07,639 --> 00:30:09,182
Why aren't you over there?

506
00:30:09,265 --> 00:30:10,433
That's over.

507
00:30:11,643 --> 00:30:13,561
-I totally messed it up.
-How?

508
00:30:14,938 --> 00:30:16,564
And how did I not know that?

509
00:30:16,648 --> 00:30:20,151
Well, because I'm me,
and I said the wrong thing, obviously.

510
00:30:21,611 --> 00:30:23,988
And because you're barely home nowadays.

511
00:30:25,198 --> 00:30:27,158
Okay, first off,

512
00:30:28,493 --> 00:30:29,869
Erin really likes you.

513
00:30:30,662 --> 00:30:31,496
Okay?

514
00:30:31,579 --> 00:30:34,916
And second, you gotta stop thinking
you can't just be honest with her.

515
00:30:34,999 --> 00:30:35,875
Really?

516
00:30:36,876 --> 00:30:39,963
Cole Walter is lecturing me
about honesty with girls.

517
00:30:40,046 --> 00:30:42,715
Yep, you're right. No more advice from me.

518
00:30:44,509 --> 00:30:45,677
Except this.

519
00:30:48,137 --> 00:30:50,348
Don't let her go
just because you didn't try.

520
00:30:55,728 --> 00:30:58,565
I am not okay

521
00:30:58,648 --> 00:31:01,150
I'm barely getting by

522
00:31:01,651 --> 00:31:04,863
I'm losing track of days

523
00:31:04,946 --> 00:31:07,240
And losing sleep at night

524
00:31:08,157 --> 00:31:10,660
I am not okay

525
00:31:11,160 --> 00:31:14,163
I'm hanging on the rails

526
00:31:14,247 --> 00:31:15,164
So if I say…

527
00:31:15,248 --> 00:31:18,585
I've got some snowflake ornaments there
that I made.

528
00:31:20,295 --> 00:31:21,504
Yeah.

529
00:31:21,588 --> 00:31:23,882
I know I can't

530
00:31:23,965 --> 00:31:26,384
Be the only one

531
00:31:27,343 --> 00:31:30,138
Who's holding on for dear life

532
00:31:30,221 --> 00:31:31,306
Yeah. Thanks.

533
00:31:33,474 --> 00:31:36,102
And God knows I know…

534
00:31:36,185 --> 00:31:37,812
Congratulations on the win.

535
00:31:39,022 --> 00:31:39,856
I didn't play.

536
00:31:41,024 --> 00:31:44,360
-Why not?
-Because I wanna be my own person.

537
00:31:46,821 --> 00:31:48,990
Does that mean
you aren't going to the showcase?

538
00:31:49,073 --> 00:31:50,408
What will your dad say?

539
00:31:50,491 --> 00:31:51,993
Yeah, I don't know.

540
00:31:52,535 --> 00:31:53,661
I guess I'll find out.

541
00:31:55,788 --> 00:31:57,332
But that's not important right now.

542
00:31:57,957 --> 00:32:00,668
What's important is that you were right.

543
00:32:01,753 --> 00:32:03,004
About what?

544
00:32:04,297 --> 00:32:08,801
Hi, everybody. Welcome. Thank you all
for coming to the Silver Falls Sparkle.

545
00:32:14,474 --> 00:32:17,769
And now it's time for the annual
Silver Falls Sparkler Awards.

546
00:32:17,852 --> 00:32:19,938
Look, I do need to take responsibility.

547
00:32:20,021 --> 00:32:21,940
And, uh, yeah, I'm gonna…

548
00:32:22,857 --> 00:32:24,776
I'm gonna figure it out, okay?

549
00:32:26,110 --> 00:32:27,236
I know you will.

550
00:32:28,404 --> 00:32:31,115
And that's why you should listen to me
'cause I'm always right.

551
00:32:32,492 --> 00:32:34,911
This year, for the first time,

552
00:32:35,411 --> 00:32:38,122
we are giving a Young Sparkler Award,

553
00:32:38,206 --> 00:32:41,334
nominated by the junior class
of Silver Falls High.

554
00:32:43,670 --> 00:32:45,713
For services to the school,

555
00:32:45,797 --> 00:32:48,883
including saving the canceled Fall Formal

556
00:32:48,967 --> 00:32:50,802
and arranging for colleges

557
00:32:50,885 --> 00:32:54,013
from all over the country
to meet with Silver Falls students.

558
00:32:54,764 --> 00:32:55,974
Jackie Howard!

559
00:32:56,808 --> 00:32:58,434
Jackie, come on up here.

560
00:32:59,936 --> 00:33:02,814
-Go, Jackie!
-You deserve it, Jackie!

561
00:33:03,314 --> 00:33:05,108
-Whoo!
-Whoo!

562
00:33:05,191 --> 00:33:06,359
You go, girl!

563
00:33:08,027 --> 00:33:08,861
Wait.

564
00:33:12,323 --> 00:33:15,243
-Did you know about this?
-You go, girl!

565
00:33:15,326 --> 00:33:18,121
Now, please join me
in showing our appreciation

566
00:33:18,204 --> 00:33:21,082
to all of our Silver Falls Sparklers!

567
00:33:29,132 --> 00:33:32,552
You know,
I don't know anyone like you, Kiley.

568
00:33:32,635 --> 00:33:35,471
Well, you've been hanging out
with cheerleaders for far too long.

569
00:33:35,555 --> 00:33:38,433
Wait, let me speak.
I'm trying to… say something.

570
00:33:40,601 --> 00:33:41,644
Okay.

571
00:33:42,145 --> 00:33:46,149
And finally,
the moment we've all been waiting for.

572
00:33:46,232 --> 00:33:48,359
I think you're pretty cool, Kiley.

573
00:33:57,076 --> 00:34:00,705
And I think I'm a little bit crazy
about you.

574
00:34:01,414 --> 00:34:03,291
Well, you're definitely crazy.

575
00:34:07,670 --> 00:34:08,963
Oh!

576
00:34:13,176 --> 00:34:14,635
Oh my God.

577
00:34:17,388 --> 00:34:18,806
Great.

578
00:34:22,602 --> 00:34:23,644
They came.

579
00:34:23,728 --> 00:34:25,646
-And tried to get us to just eat--
-Erin?

580
00:34:31,778 --> 00:34:32,737
Look, uh,

581
00:34:33,321 --> 00:34:36,949
I get that you don't see a future with me,
and that's fine.

582
00:34:37,033 --> 00:34:38,367
-Really.
-No, it's not…

583
00:34:39,118 --> 00:34:40,119
That's not it.

584
00:34:42,080 --> 00:34:43,664
We're so young,

585
00:34:43,748 --> 00:34:46,667
and I think we might be headed
in different directions.

586
00:34:47,168 --> 00:34:48,628
And I do believe in you.

587
00:34:49,212 --> 00:34:51,839
You should go after your dreams,
but so should I.

588
00:34:53,341 --> 00:34:54,175
Yeah.

589
00:34:54,258 --> 00:34:56,177
I don't want to be the girl
that held you back.

590
00:34:56,260 --> 00:34:57,970
I would never think of you like that.

591
00:34:58,054 --> 00:35:01,974
And you're right,
our dreams… are different,

592
00:35:02,058 --> 00:35:03,226
but that's okay.

593
00:35:06,104 --> 00:35:08,314
So why don't we just try to enjoy
what we have for now?

594
00:35:09,398 --> 00:35:11,859
You know, we can worry
about the future when it's here.

595
00:35:12,985 --> 00:35:14,070
I'd like that.

596
00:35:15,780 --> 00:35:16,614
Yeah.

597
00:35:17,406 --> 00:35:18,324
All right.

598
00:35:31,170 --> 00:35:34,006
Hope floats

599
00:35:35,424 --> 00:35:38,386
Up and down the Pacific coast

600
00:35:38,469 --> 00:35:40,763
Ooh, faith

601
00:35:41,389 --> 00:35:43,391
Needs

602
00:35:43,975 --> 00:35:46,936
Best, it's best to set ourselves free

603
00:35:47,019 --> 00:35:48,229
Ooh

604
00:35:48,312 --> 00:35:49,939
When we stick together

605
00:35:50,022 --> 00:35:51,983
The light is found

606
00:35:52,066 --> 00:35:54,944
Tell me now or never
We're safe and sound…

607
00:35:55,027 --> 00:35:55,862
Breathing.

608
00:35:55,945 --> 00:35:56,779
Hey!

609
00:35:56,863 --> 00:35:58,614
When we stick together…

610
00:35:59,198 --> 00:36:00,616
One, two, three.

611
00:36:04,495 --> 00:36:05,371
Thanks, Terry.

612
00:36:06,247 --> 00:36:07,165
Cheers.

613
00:36:10,042 --> 00:36:12,128
Oh, hi! Can I see it?

614
00:36:12,211 --> 00:36:13,212
Yeah.

615
00:36:13,963 --> 00:36:15,256
Oh!

616
00:36:15,339 --> 00:36:17,091
I hope you know how much you deserve this.

617
00:36:17,842 --> 00:36:18,801
Yeah, well.

618
00:36:19,302 --> 00:36:24,348
Listen, I know that the last few months
haven't exactly been easy for you, but

619
00:36:25,683 --> 00:36:28,603
you're such a huge part
of this community and our family.

620
00:36:30,938 --> 00:36:32,648
Thanks for coming back to us.

621
00:36:33,691 --> 00:36:36,110
Thank you for persuading me
to come back to you.

622
00:36:36,194 --> 00:36:38,196
I'm just glad
that everything's working out.

623
00:36:38,279 --> 00:36:41,324
I mean, it almost feels like
everything's getting back to normal.

624
00:36:41,407 --> 00:36:43,701
We're safe and sound

625
00:36:43,784 --> 00:36:45,870
When we stick together…

626
00:36:50,458 --> 00:36:51,626
There she is.

627
00:36:51,709 --> 00:36:52,543
One sec.

628
00:36:54,629 --> 00:36:56,672
Jackie, congrats on the award.

629
00:36:57,465 --> 00:36:58,299
Thanks.

630
00:36:59,258 --> 00:37:00,176
Was it you?

631
00:37:01,219 --> 00:37:02,386
No.

632
00:37:03,179 --> 00:37:04,555
And I'm sworn to secrecy.

633
00:37:11,938 --> 00:37:14,523
I think you should go for
student council president next year.

634
00:37:14,607 --> 00:37:17,652
What? No. I tried running
for junior class president.

635
00:37:17,735 --> 00:37:21,280
-And look how well that turned out.
-Everyone knows who should've won.

636
00:37:22,198 --> 00:37:23,699
And anyways,

637
00:37:23,783 --> 00:37:26,285
I think you'll have a pretty easy run
at student council president

638
00:37:26,369 --> 00:37:29,622
because I'm gonna make you VP
as of next semester.

639
00:37:31,082 --> 00:37:32,875
-You can do that?
-Sure.

640
00:37:35,127 --> 00:37:36,003
Thanks.

641
00:37:36,671 --> 00:37:37,713
You deserve it.

642
00:37:38,464 --> 00:37:41,342
It's good. I'm proud of you.

643
00:37:41,425 --> 00:37:43,261
Let's see what happens next.

644
00:37:47,932 --> 00:37:48,933
Hey.

645
00:37:51,352 --> 00:37:52,186
Hey.

646
00:37:55,648 --> 00:37:57,149
I'm just gonna, uh…

647
00:37:58,943 --> 00:38:00,486
Hey, Erin, wait up.

648
00:38:00,987 --> 00:38:02,530
Uh, congratulations.

649
00:38:02,613 --> 00:38:04,740
Yeah. Thanks.

650
00:38:04,824 --> 00:38:05,741
Um…

651
00:38:06,993 --> 00:38:08,619
-You too.
-Thanks.

652
00:38:11,497 --> 00:38:12,748
Are you happy?

653
00:38:13,916 --> 00:38:14,750
I am.

654
00:38:16,294 --> 00:38:18,087
It, uh… it felt good this time.

655
00:38:18,170 --> 00:38:20,464
Great. That's great.

656
00:38:27,179 --> 00:38:28,306
I, um…

657
00:38:30,433 --> 00:38:32,643
I'll see you at home. Okay?

658
00:38:35,396 --> 00:38:36,230
Okay.

659
00:38:46,907 --> 00:38:49,243
I just don't think I can get past this.

660
00:38:50,578 --> 00:38:53,289
I invested everything into this project.

661
00:38:54,123 --> 00:38:55,750
I really wanted it to work.

662
00:38:57,501 --> 00:39:00,671
I think it would've worked.
But now it's just gone.

663
00:39:01,714 --> 00:39:03,466
And my dad took it away.

664
00:39:03,549 --> 00:39:04,425
Yeah.

665
00:39:06,260 --> 00:39:08,012
What am I supposed to do now?

666
00:39:10,598 --> 00:39:15,019
You know, the… the farm I was at
was in the middle of nowhere.

667
00:39:15,102 --> 00:39:18,856
And we slept in tents,
and some days there was no electricity,

668
00:39:18,939 --> 00:39:20,649
and other days the food would run low,

669
00:39:20,733 --> 00:39:23,819
and we would just hope
that supply trucks were on their way.

670
00:39:23,903 --> 00:39:26,614
-Yeah. Yeah, I know. It sounded awful.
-No.

671
00:39:26,697 --> 00:39:28,491
No, it was great.

672
00:39:29,575 --> 00:39:32,745
Not when the toilet was backed up
for three days. That was awful.

673
00:39:32,828 --> 00:39:34,830
But most of the time.

674
00:39:37,083 --> 00:39:41,837
There is a whole world out there,
and we haven't seen any of it.

675
00:39:44,548 --> 00:39:46,092
What if this town is

676
00:39:47,343 --> 00:39:49,678
just too small for your big ideas?

677
00:40:02,566 --> 00:40:04,652
-Danny, go.
-I'll teach you about a C chord.

678
00:40:04,735 --> 00:40:07,571
-The C chord?
-It's the most basic chord.

679
00:40:07,655 --> 00:40:10,199
-It's your turn.
-I know how to do an ollie.

680
00:40:11,534 --> 00:40:14,787
-Uh, hey, Jackie, you want to sit here?
-Yeah, thanks.

681
00:40:14,870 --> 00:40:16,455
Why not try and do an ollie?

682
00:40:18,165 --> 00:40:21,961
Hey, can I interview you
for my People of Influence assignment?

683
00:40:22,044 --> 00:40:23,879
-Sure, Jordan.
-Thanks.

684
00:40:24,672 --> 00:40:26,090
How much can you really learn…

685
00:40:26,173 --> 00:40:29,385
So… now that you passed your driving test…

686
00:40:30,177 --> 00:40:33,013
I'll soon be your own personal chauffeur,
just like I promised.

687
00:40:33,931 --> 00:40:35,391
-Okay.
-Do you have any twos?

688
00:40:36,183 --> 00:40:37,685
Hey, guys, is Mom around?

689
00:40:37,768 --> 00:40:40,312
-She had to go out on a call.
-And where's Dad?

690
00:40:40,396 --> 00:40:42,940
-He's up on the top field.
-At this time of night?

691
00:40:43,023 --> 00:40:44,775
Yeah, he's been up there all afternoon.

692
00:40:45,651 --> 00:40:48,487
Thanks. Hey, and congrats.

693
00:40:49,238 --> 00:40:51,365
Appreciate you guys. All of you.

694
00:40:53,117 --> 00:40:56,537
Hey, while we're congratulating everyone,
Cole got his new SAT scores.

695
00:40:57,705 --> 00:40:59,582
Cole? What did you get?

696
00:41:00,374 --> 00:41:02,001
Just like a 1250.

697
00:41:02,084 --> 00:41:04,545
That's amazing. When did you get them?

698
00:41:04,628 --> 00:41:05,671
Couple weeks ago.

699
00:41:05,754 --> 00:41:07,423
But I… I thought…

700
00:41:12,052 --> 00:41:13,762
Why didn't you say anything?

701
00:41:14,346 --> 00:41:17,183
You know what? Um, you guys celebrate.

702
00:41:17,266 --> 00:41:18,267
I'm going out.

703
00:41:28,110 --> 00:41:28,944
Cole?

704
00:41:31,822 --> 00:41:32,781
Are you okay?

705
00:41:34,575 --> 00:41:35,576
I'm fine.

706
00:41:38,162 --> 00:41:40,080
Can we not do this again?

707
00:41:40,789 --> 00:41:42,166
I know you're not fine.

708
00:41:43,501 --> 00:41:45,127
You've been off with me for weeks.

709
00:41:45,211 --> 00:41:47,546
You've been avoiding me,
staying out of the house,

710
00:41:47,630 --> 00:41:49,798
and we were supposed to do
college applications together,

711
00:41:49,882 --> 00:41:52,343
but you don't tell me
you got your SAT scores?

712
00:41:53,135 --> 00:41:55,679
Just, please, be honest with me.

713
00:41:57,264 --> 00:42:00,226
Oh, like you've been honest with me?

714
00:42:00,309 --> 00:42:01,769
What are you talking about?

715
00:42:02,269 --> 00:42:04,104
I have been honest with you.

716
00:42:04,188 --> 00:42:06,732
I don't think
you've even been honest with yourself.

717
00:42:07,233 --> 00:42:08,275
Okay, Cole.

718
00:42:09,818 --> 00:42:10,653
Okay.

719
00:42:11,654 --> 00:42:13,030
Here's some honesty for you.

720
00:42:15,533 --> 00:42:17,034
I saw you and Alex

721
00:42:18,160 --> 00:42:19,245
at Richard's.

722
00:42:23,082 --> 00:42:24,041
You know,

723
00:42:24,542 --> 00:42:27,169
I was giving you space, like you asked.

724
00:42:27,753 --> 00:42:30,005
But I thought we had something.
I've been racking my brain

725
00:42:30,089 --> 00:42:32,508
trying to understand why
you'd be with my brother again.

726
00:42:32,591 --> 00:42:35,344
We said that we were going to be friends.

727
00:42:35,427 --> 00:42:36,929
We've never just been friends.

728
00:42:37,012 --> 00:42:38,597
Cole, this is not…

729
00:42:39,723 --> 00:42:41,350
-Me and Alex, we're--
-What?

730
00:42:41,934 --> 00:42:45,771
Why is it you can't stay away from him,
but youcanstay away from me?

731
00:42:47,773 --> 00:42:51,944
I can't… stay away from you, okay?

732
00:42:52,778 --> 00:42:55,948
I keep trying to, and nothing works.

733
00:42:56,448 --> 00:42:58,284
And I… I can't have that, Cole.

734
00:42:58,367 --> 00:43:03,163
I can't be with someone who makes me feel
the way that you make me feel.

735
00:43:03,789 --> 00:43:05,916
-How do I make you feel?
-Stop it.

736
00:43:06,000 --> 00:43:08,252
I love you, Jackie.

737
00:43:09,962 --> 00:43:13,549
And I thought you felt the same way,
but if I'm wrong, then just… just say it.

738
00:43:21,265 --> 00:43:22,433
I love you.

739
00:43:23,267 --> 00:43:24,310
Okay?

740
00:43:24,393 --> 00:43:26,729
Are we done? Can I go now?

741
00:43:26,812 --> 00:43:29,106
Why would being with me be so awful?

742
00:43:32,484 --> 00:43:33,736
What is it?

743
00:43:34,695 --> 00:43:36,697
When we kissed before,

744
00:43:36,780 --> 00:43:41,118
it was the only time that I've ever
stopped thinking about everything.

745
00:43:41,201 --> 00:43:45,914
How I'm doing in school, if I fit in here,
what my future will look like.

746
00:43:45,998 --> 00:43:48,417
I felt really… free,

747
00:43:49,418 --> 00:43:54,048
like I was out of control,
and… and I can't have that, Cole.

748
00:43:54,131 --> 00:43:56,842
I can't. I can't lose control.

749
00:43:57,509 --> 00:43:58,344
Why?

750
00:43:59,803 --> 00:44:00,721
Because…

751
00:44:00,804 --> 00:44:03,015
My mother said I'm too romantic…

752
00:44:03,098 --> 00:44:05,434
I don't know what might happen if I do.

753
00:44:08,979 --> 00:44:12,107
I only started to believe her…

754
00:44:13,108 --> 00:44:14,443
You love him?

755
00:44:16,445 --> 00:44:18,364
I don't say…

756
00:44:18,447 --> 00:44:19,490
Alex…

757
00:44:19,990 --> 00:44:22,743
But still you take my breath

758
00:44:22,826 --> 00:44:25,454
And still the things I know…

759
00:44:25,537 --> 00:44:27,289
Hey, what's going on?

760
00:44:28,957 --> 00:44:30,209
It's Dad.

761
00:44:30,292 --> 00:44:33,462
From out of the cold

762
00:44:34,713 --> 00:44:36,840
Fire on fire

763
00:44:36,924 --> 00:44:38,509
Would normally kill us

764
00:44:38,592 --> 00:44:40,719
But this much desire

765
00:44:40,803 --> 00:44:42,805
Together we're winners

766
00:44:42,888 --> 00:44:45,099
They say that we're out of control

767
00:44:45,182 --> 00:44:46,725
And some say we're sinners

768
00:44:46,809 --> 00:44:49,103
But don't let them ruin

769
00:44:49,186 --> 00:44:51,188
Our beautiful rhythms

770
00:44:51,271 --> 00:44:53,315
'Cause when you unfold me

771
00:44:53,399 --> 00:44:55,526
And tell me you love me

772
00:44:55,609 --> 00:44:58,237
Then look in my eyes

773
00:44:59,988 --> 00:45:01,532
You are perfection

774
00:45:01,615 --> 00:45:03,784
My only direction

775
00:45:03,867 --> 00:45:06,495
It's fire on fire

776
00:45:08,205 --> 00:45:13,001
You are perfection, my only direction

777
00:45:14,086 --> 00:45:18,716
